---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { contactEmail, site } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What data taranity.com collects, how it's handled, and your rights — in plain language."
>
  <article class="legal">
    <p class="band-label mono-label">/ privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="legal-lead">
      Plain language, no dark patterns. This site belongs to {site.name}, a digital studio
      ({site.url}). It sets <strong>no cookies</strong> and shows no consent banner because it
      doesn't need one. Here's exactly what happens with your data.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>What we collect, and when</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>The contact form.</strong> Only if you submit it: your name, email, and message.
          It's delivered to us through <a href="https://web3forms.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Web3Forms</a>
          (a form-to-email service acting as a processor) and used <em>solely</em> to reply. It is
          never sold, shared for marketing, or added to any list.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Analytics.</strong> If analytics are enabled, the site uses
          <a href="https://plausible.io/data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Plausible</a>
          — privacy-first, cookieless, fully aggregated, with no personal data and no cross-site
          tracking. Nothing identifies you.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The "Currently" widget.</strong> Our latest commit is fetched once when the site
          is <em>built</em>, not from your browser — so no request to GitHub is made on your behalf
          and your IP is never shared. The local-time readout is computed entirely in your browser.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Hosting.</strong> The site is served by Cloudflare Pages. Like any web host, it
          processes connection data (such as your IP) in transient server logs to deliver the site
          and protect against abuse.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Booking link.</strong> If you choose to book a call, you're taken to an external
          scheduling service; its own privacy policy applies once you're there.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>None. This site stores nothing on your device for tracking, and there is no advertising.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under the GDPR you can ask to access, correct, or delete the personal data we hold about you,
        or object to its processing. In practice the only data we ever hold is the message you chose
        to send us — so a deletion request simply means we delete that email. Email
        <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a> and we'll handle it promptly.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Retention</h2>
      <p>
        Contact messages are kept only as long as needed to deal with your enquiry, then deleted.
        Analytics data (if enabled) is aggregated and never tied to an individual.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="legal-meta mono-label">Last reviewed: June 2026 · Questions? {contactEmail}</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 8rem var(--spacing-gutter) var(--spacing-section);
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
  }
  .band-label { color: var(--color-cyan); margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .legal h1 { font-size: var(--text-h1); margin-bottom: 1.4rem; }
  .legal-lead { font-size: var(--text-lead); color: var(--color-ink); line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .legal section { margin-bottom: 2.2rem; }
  .legal h2 { font-size: var(--text-h3); margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }
  .legal p { color: var(--color-ink-dim); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 0.8rem; }
  .legal ul { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 1rem; }
  .legal li { color: var(--color-ink-dim); line-height: 1.65; padding-left: 1.1rem; position: relative; }
  .legal li::before { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0.65em; width: 6px; height: 6px; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--color-cyan); }
  .legal strong { color: var(--color-ink); }
  .legal a { color: var(--color-cyan); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  .legal-meta { margin-top: 2.5rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line); color: var(--color-ink-faint); }
</style>
